BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261103T230000Z
DTEND:20261104T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20261103T000000Z
SUMMARY:Nic Cage Film Discussion Group
DESCRIPTION:*NOVEMBER'S DISCUSSION WILL BE HELD OFFSITE AT WELDON MILLS\n\n 
 \n\nWeldon Mills  \n\n300 E Main St Ste 001\, Durham\, NC 27701 \n\nThe 
 entrance is off North Roxboro Street. \n\nWeldon Mills is a five-minute 
 walk from the library straight down North Roxboro Street. \n\n\n\nParking 
 is available in the library parking lot or the North Queen Street Garage 
 located at 115 North Queen Street which is located directly across the 
 street from the library behind the apartments. Parking in the garage is 
 free. Please bring your parking ticket to a service point for validation. 
 You can validate your ticket before the program.   \n\nParking at the 
 library may be limited due to Election Day voting at Main.  \n\nOther 
 parking options for Weldon Mills \n\n \n\n \n\nThe man... The myth... The 
 legend... \n\nNIC CAGE! \n\n\n\nA film career that has spanned decades and 
 genres\, blockbusters and direct to video\, Nic Cage is a force unto 
 himself. \n\nIncomparable practicing his own style of method acting which 
 he calls Nouveau shamanism he transcends acting conventions. \n\nThe only 
 actor meta enough to have played himself. The only actor to have become an 
 internet meme. The only actor to have a library film discussion group 
 devoted to him.  \n\n \n\n\n\nEach month we will discuss a different film 
 from Nic Cage’s long and productive film career. \n\nFilms cover early 
 career classics like Valley Girl to later performances like Dream Scenario. 
 Please see the film schedule listed below.  \n\nThe 2027 Nic Cage Film 
 Discussion Group dates and film schedule can be found here! \n\n 
 \n\n\n\nSuggested reading for the discussion group all of which are 
 available through the library catalogue or interlibrary loan:   \n\n\n	Age 
 of Cage: Four Decades of Hollywood Through One Singular Career by Keith 
 Phipps  \n	National Treasure: Nicolas Cage by Lindsay Gibb (ISBN-13: 
 ‎978-1770412361)  \n	How Coppola Became Cage by Zach Schonfeld (ISBN-13 : 
 978-0197556375)\n\n\n \n\nAll Nic Cage materials at the library can be 
 found in the Durham County Library Online Catalog \n\nCheck out Nic Cage 
 Films Based on a Book! \n\nThanks to generous donations from patrons the 
 following films have been added to the collection: Red Rock West\, The 
 Rock\, Gone in Sixty Seconds and Con Air!\n\nNot sure if the film is right 
 for you? Check out Does the Dog Die? for information on content in the 
 films. May contain spoilers on the films.  \n\n \n\n\n\nDidn’t watch the 
 film? That’s ok! Feel free to join as Nic Cage transcends discussions 
 about specific films! \n\n \n\nRefreshments will be served however please 
 bring your own covered beverage.  \n\n \n\nFirst Tuesday of the month\, 
 excluding April\, starting at 6 pm in the Children's Programming Room on 
 the second floor of the Durham County Main Library located at 300 North 
 Roxboro Street.  \n\n*January's Discussion Group will be in the Main 
 Library Auditorium \n\nParking is available in the library parking lot or 
 the North Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street which is 
 located directly across the street from the library behind the apartments. 
 Parking in the garage is free. Please bring your parking ticket to a 
 service point for validation.  \n\nRegistration is appreciated but not 
 required. Register to receive email reminders.  \n\n \n\n\n\nSchedule of 
 films for 2026: \n\nJanuary 6 – Vampire’s Kiss \n\nFebruary 3 – 
 Valley Girl \n\nMarch 3 – Wild At Heart \n\nApril – No discussion group 
 \n\nMay 5 – Raising Arizona \n\nJune 2 – Dream Scenario \n\nJuly 7 – 
 Con Air \n\nAugust 4 – Leaving Las Vegas \n\nSeptember 1 – Gone in 60 
 Seconds  \n\nOctober 6 – Willy’s Wonderland \n\nNovember 3 – The Rock 
 \n\nDecember 1 – Matchstick Men  \n\n \n\nQuestions? Contact 
 mkoslofsky@dconc.gov \n\n \n\nImage description: Actor Nicolas Cage poses 
 on the red carpet at the Venice Film Festival\, showcasing his signature 
 style and charisma.\n\n\n\nPhoto credit: Georges Biard
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan Koslofsky":MAILTO:mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Durham, Movie, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-15314199
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/15314199
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261103T233000Z
DTEND:20261104T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261103T000000Z
SUMMARY:Big Kid Storytime
DESCRIPTION:Geared toward kids and tweens\, ages 7-12! Join us every 
 Tuesday evening for the next chapter in our selected chapter book reading! 
 A snack will be served.\n\nListening to books has serious benefits for 
 developing readers. It helps tweens improve their pronunciation and 
 fluency\, improves focus and memory\, increases attention span\, builds 
 comprehension skills\, and can boost mental health by relieving stress and 
 calming thoughts. A small snack will be served. For kids\, teens\, and 
 tweens\, ages 7 and up! \n\n \n\n \n\n \n\n
LOCATION:Southwest Regional - Children's Programming Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline P.":MAILTO:cbpeterson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Story Time
