SUMMARY:Celebrate Diwali at the Library!
DESCRIPTION:Diwali (or Deepavali meaning “rows of lighted lamps”) is 
 one of the largest holidays celebrated in India and parts of South Asia. 
 Widely known as the “festival of lights\,” Diwali is celebrated by 
 Hindus\, Sikhs\, and Jains all marking different historical events as the 
 origins for the holiday with the common theme of good overcoming evil or 
 light overcoming darkness. Diwali traditionally involves lighting oil lamps 
 (“diyas”) in homes\, creating rangoli designs in the streets\, lighting 
 fireworks\, and eating large feasts with family and friends including 
 sweets known as ‘mithai.’ The festival lasts five days and is typically 
 celebrated in October or November\, depending on the position of the moon. 
 \n\nCome learn about and celebrate Diwali at the library with the Duke AAPI 
 Affinity Group – we’ll read books on the festival followed by a few 
 arts and crafts activities!\n\nAll ages welcome. No registration required. 
 Questions? Email kstockdale@dconc.gov or call (919) 560-8592.
LOCATION:Southwest Meeting Room\, Southwest Regional Library (3605 Shannon Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Kristen Stockdale":MAILTO:kstockdale@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Arts & Crafts, Story Time
UID:LibCal-14288-17456543
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17456543
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261107T150000Z
DTEND:20261107T163000Z
DTSTAMP:20261107T000000Z
SUMMARY:Mindful Yoga
DESCRIPTION:Inhale\, exhale\, and join us for a Mindful Yoga class at 
 Durham East Regional Library! Start your Saturday with an hour of gentle 
 hatha yoga\, then stick around from 11:00 to 11:30 for tea and conversation 
 with your neighbors.\n\nThis class offers a slower\, reflective approach to 
 yoga that integrates gentle movement\, breathwork\, rest\, and brief 
 exploration of yogic philosophy. Expect an accessible\, non-strenuous 
 practice that emphasizes steadiness\, ease\, and mindfulness — both on 
 and off the mat.\n\nPlease bring a yoga mat and a mug for tea to use at the 
 program. Spare yoga mats are available while supplies last. Space is 
 limited. Registration is required.\n\nIf you have questions about 
 accessibility and/or need accommodations\, please contact Mara (she/her): 
 mplantholt@dconc.gov or 919-560-0207.\n\n\nAbout the presenter:\n\nRohini 
 Rajgopal is a certified yoga instructor trained through Kaivalyadhama\, one 
 of India’s oldest yoga institutes. Her teaching is rooted in classical 
 yogic principles and emphasizes yoga as a holistic practice — not just 
 physical postures — creating space for reflection\, breath\, and embodied 
 awareness.
LOCATION:East Meeting Room\, East Regional Library (211 Lick Creek Lane)
ORGANIZER;CN="Mara Plantholt":MAILTO:mplantholt@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Health & Fitness
UID:LibCal-14288-17693055
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17693055
