SUMMARY:Bite into Science
DESCRIPTION:Join us for an interactive series to discover the exciting 
 world of nutrition\, healthy habits\, and food science! Through hands-on 
 experiments\, engaging demonstrations\, games\, and creative activities\, 
 kids will learn how their bodies use food for energy\, why healthy choices 
 matter\, and how science is all around us. Each session is designed to 
 spark curiosity\, encourage healthy lifestyles\, and make learning fun. No 
 prior science experience is needed—just bring your curiosity and get 
 ready to explore!\n\nAbout the presenters: Sophie and Yoojin are Duke 
 undergraduate students interested in pursuing careers in medicine who are 
 passionate about promoting nutrition and wellness through early education. 
 They enjoy making science fun while inspiring young learners to build 
 healthy habits that can last a lifetime.
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Christina Economou":MAILTO:ceconomou@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17284439
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17284439
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261107T153000Z
DTEND:20261107T170000Z
DTSTAMP:20261107T000000Z
SUMMARY:America 250: Surprising Stories of North Carolina in the American Revolution
DESCRIPTION:In this 250th Anniversary of the American Revolution\, North 
 Carolina residents may wonder\, “What happened here?” From the 1775 
 burning of the only fort destroyed by Patriots anywhere\, to a final 
 Redcoat raid in 1782\, our state was the scene of surprising stories from 
 the mountains to the sea. Examples include a forgotten campaign against the 
 Cherokee\, an Overmountain Campaign that turned the tide of war\, an iconic 
 chase between two armies ending in a climactic battle\, and a vicious civil 
 war between partisans. Enslaved people\, minorities\, and women all took 
 courageous stands. Within an hour’s drive of Durham\, Continentals made a 
 dramatic escape\, the governor was kidnapped\, and Tories were tricked to 
 death. Come become an instant expert on Revolutionary N.C. and you’ll 
 amaze your “kith and kin!”\n\nJim Morgan is a writer/researcher with a 
 master’s degree in journalism from the University of Missouri. Jim 
 created “The American Revolution Tour of North Carolina™” 
 (AmRevNC.com)\, a research-based\, book-length website telling the stories 
 of more than 100 locations across the state. He continues the research and 
 gives tours\, talks\, and TV interviews\, and published two articles on the 
 Revolution in the April 2026 issue of Our State magazine.\n\nE-mail Bob 
 with any questions: rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Bob S.":MAILTO:rskesler@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Author Visit, Classes & Lectures, Durham, Humanities, North Carolina Collection
UID:LibCal-14288-17552603
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17552603
END:VEVENT
