DTEND:20261110T003000Z
DTSTAMP:20261109T000000Z
SUMMARY:Mystery Book Club -- We Solve Murders
DESCRIPTION:Join us virtually or in-person to discuss We Solve Murders by 
 Richard Osman.\n\nSteve Wheeler is enjoying retired life. He does the odd 
 bit of investigation work\, but he prefers his familiar habits and 
 routines: the pub quiz\, his favorite bench\, his cat waiting for him when 
 he comes home. His days of adventure are over: adrenaline is 
 daughter-in-law Amy's business now.\n\nAmy Wheeler thinks adrenaline is 
 good for the soul. As a private security officer\, she doesn't stay still 
 long enough for habits or routines. She's currently on a remote island 
 keeping world-famous author Rosie D'Antonio alive. Which was meant to be an 
 easy job... \n\nThen a dead body\, a bag of money\, and a killer with their 
 sights on Amy have her sending an SOS to the only person she trusts. A 
 breakneck race around the world begins\, but can Amy and Steve stay one 
 step ahead of a lethal enemy?\n\nClick below for format 
 availability:\n\nDurham County\n\nOrange County\n\nChatham County\n\nWake 
 County\n\nAdditionally\, beginning Tuesday October 13th\, there will be 
 physical copies available at the North Regional Information Desk while 
 supplies last.\n\nRegistration is required to receive the Zoom link to 
 attend the event.\n\nE-mail Bob with any questions: rskesler@dconc.gov
LOCATION:North Meeting Room - Full Room\, North Regional Library (221 Milton Rd)
ORGANIZER;CN="Bob S.":MAILTO:rskesler@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17153113
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17153113
END:VEVENT
