SUMMARY:Falling for Meteor Showers (drop-in program)
DESCRIPTION:Ever wonder what meteor showers are\, what about them "falls\," 
 and why people love to observe them? Join the Maker   STEAM team in the 
 third floor Innovation Lab at Main Library for drop-in activities and 
 resources to learn more about what there is to love about meteor showers! 
 In these stations\, you can:\n\n\n	\n	Read information about meteor showers 
 to spark your curiosity\,\n	\n	\n	Take a resource list with you to explore 
 more from home\, and\n	\n	\n	Pick one or both of the meteor shower art 
 activities to complete in the Innovation Lab!\n	\n\n\nThese activities are 
 self-paced with written instructions and an example provided. These 
 activities are geared towards ages 5 and up\, all ages welcome.\n\nThis 
 program is drop-in\, no registration required. Please join us between 11am 
 and 1pm in the Innovation Lab on 3rd floor of Main Library. The activities 
 will take most participants around 15 to 30 minutes in total to complete. 
 This event is for all ages\; children under age 11 must be accompanied by 
 an adult. \n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or accommodation 
 needs\, please contact us at Maker_STEAM@dconc.gov. We ask that all 
 requests be made at least 3 business days prior to the event to ensure we 
 can provide the best accommodations possible.
LOCATION:Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Caroline Flory":MAILTO:cflory@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, High Sensory Stimulation, Maker, STEAM
