SUMMARY:Drawn to Graphic Novels: Middle School Book Club @ South Regional
DESCRIPTION:This book club is intended for middle-schoolers in grades 6-8. 
 Meets the 2nd Thursday of each month! ⭐\n\nRead\, share\, sketch\, snack! 
 Discuss great stories\, doodle\, and discover your next favorite graphic 
 novel!\n\n(Stick figures welcome\, but only sketch if you want: no art 
 skills required!)\n\nPlus\, attendees get first pick from books suggested 
 by our Teen Librarian for the next month’s meeting! 📖\n\nThis 
 meeting's theme will be Fantasy Worlds - kids who enjoy Amulet or Wings of 
 Fire are going to enjoy this session! Kids can prepare by reading any 
 graphic novel featuring dragons\, mermaids\, castles and knights\, magic 
 and mystique - check out this booklist if you need ideas for your next 
 read!\n\n🧙‍♂️✨🐉🏰🌙\n\nQuestions? Email Ezra\, South 
 Regional's Teen Librarian\, at eletson@dconc.gov
LOCATION:South Regional - Children's Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Ezra L.":MAILTO:eletson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Book Club, Social
