SUMMARY:Make It: Paper
DESCRIPTION:The holidays are coming. Have you thought about making gifts 
 this year? Combine your creativity and the library's maker tools and space 
 to make something one of a kind! We'll provide supplies\, inspiration\, and 
 support. \n\nNeed some solo time to work on a project of your own? Bring 
 your materials\, grab a seat\, and use us as an excuse! \n\nMaybe you have 
 a lot going on and just need to pause for a bit? Crafting is an excellent 
 brain break\, and you should do nice things for yourself. \n\nFeel free to 
 drop in and stay as long as you need/want. This session\, we'll make 
 paper!\n\nInterested in using the 3D printer\, laser cutter\, or Cricut 
 machine for your projects? Take the required online\, self-paced trainings 
 first. We're happy to help you from there!\n\n\nNovember 13\, 3-5p: making 
 paper\n\nNovember 18\, 5-7p: making earrings\n\nDecember 4\, 3-5p: making 
 window clings\n\nDecember 9\, 3-7p cat & dog toys\n\nDecember 11\, 4-5p: 
 making bird feeders\, a joint program with Getting Ready for Christmas Bird 
 Count\n\nDecember 19\, 11a-1p and 3-5p: TBD
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
