SUMMARY:Acting Workshop
DESCRIPTION:Did you enjoy our Acting Workshop this past summer? Or maybe 
 you didn't get a chance to go? Come join us for a fun and hands-on acting 
 class in the 2nd Floor Programming Room! This program is designed for all 
 ages and all levels of acting experience. Whether you've been acting your 
 whole life or have never done it before\, this program will be a safe and 
 silly space for all of us to get up on our feet and try all sorts of 
 exciting things. Look forward to some vocal and body warm-ups\, lots of 
 improv exercises and some brief scene work. See you there!
LOCATION:Main Children's Programming Room\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Miles Simpson-Quigley":MAILTO:msquigley@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Other
