BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261116T230000Z
DTEND:20261117T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261116T000000Z
SUMMARY:Is this AI? Spotting Misinformation Online
DESCRIPTION:It is almost impossible to be online today without encountering 
 content generated by artificial intelligence (AI). Whether you are looking 
 for the latest news\, scrolling through posts on social media\, or looking 
 up a new recipe for dinner\, AI has made it more difficult to tell if what 
 we see online can be trusted. \n\nThis presentation will cover some of the 
 clues we can look for to determine if something has been generated by AI 
 and help you learn skills to verify the information you find online.
LOCATION:South Meeting Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="James McKinnell":MAILTO:jmckinnell@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Digital/Tech Literacy
UID:LibCal-14288-17837154
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17837154
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20261116T230000Z
DTEND:20261117T000000Z
DTSTAMP:20261116T000000Z
SUMMARY:Shakedown on Sugar
DESCRIPTION:Sugar makes food taste good\, but it can have some not so sweet 
 effects on our health. Let’s learn about the different types of sugars in 
 our food and how much may be too much. Knowing about the sugars in our 
 foods and setting healthy limits may help us find the sweet spot between 
 enjoyment/well-being and health/wellness.\n\nBy attending this program you 
 can earn an extra entry into the One Walk to Rule Them All grand prize 
 raffle with submission of a completed tracker. \n\nOne Walk to Rule Them 
 All was made possible through the generosity of the Friends of the Durham 
 Library.\n\n
LOCATION:Adult Programming Room\, South Regional Library (4505 S. Alston Ave)
ORGANIZER;CN="Jessica L.":MAILTO:jllundin@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Friends of the Durham Library, Health & Fitness, One Walk
UID:LibCal-14288-17654572
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17654572
END:VEVENT
