SUMMARY:Library Taskmaster!
DESCRIPTION:Library Taskmaster!* Community Engagement is bringing the 
 highly popular comedy hit Taskmaster to the library. This adults-only 
 program will feature games from the show\, and the winner will receive a 
 very special prize!\n\nWe will host adults (age 21 ) in the auditorium to 
 compete. These are silly\, low-stakes games that require wit and 
 creativity. By the end of the evening\, one sole winner will emerge as the 
 first ever Library Taskmaster Champion.\n\nFor a chance to participate\, 
 you will be given a number at the door. Our magic number picker will 
 determine who plays what game. Five games featuring five different 
 contestants per game will lead to a LIVE FINAL where the winners of the 
 previous five tasks will compete for TASKMASTER GLORY. \n\nRegistration is 
 appreciated to receive an email reminder\, cancellation link\, and program 
 updates. Seating is first come first served. Registration does not hold or 
 guarantee a seat.\n\nQuestions? Email jjamsky@dconc.gov or 
 sgibson@dconc.gov.\n\n*not affiliated with actual Taskmaster 
 (unfortunately)\n\nIf you have any accessibility questions or accommodation 
 needs\, please contact Jennifer at Accessibility_Services@dconc.gov. We ask 
 that\, if possible\, all accommodation requests be made at least three (3) 
 business days prior to the event.
LOCATION:Main Auditorium\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Sara Gibson":MAILTO:sgibson@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Accommodations Available, Community Engagement, High Sensory Stimulation
