SUMMARY:Laptop Distribution Initiative
DESCRIPTION:The City of Durham\, Digital Inclusion Services Team is 
 launching our Laptop Distribution Initiative. Eligible Durham residents 
 will be provided with a free refurbished laptop\, 90 days of free technical 
 support\, and free anti-virus/malware software pre-installed\, offered 
 through partner Kramden Institute.\n\nClick on the link below for more 
 information and to apply. If you qualify to receive a laptop\, our team 
 will contact you with additional information and pickup dates. \n\n 
 \n\n\n	\n	Applicants must meet income limitations or currently be enrolled 
 in income-based government assistance programs. \n	\n	\n	Must be a 
 Durham/Durham County Resident \n	\n	\n	Applicants must be able to provide 
 Photo ID and proof of eligibility by bringing qualifying documents at the 
 time of pickup \n	\n	\n	Must be at least 18 years of age\n	\n	\n	One survey 
 per household\n	\n\n\nApply with the Laptop Distribution Initiative 
 Application\n\nFor any additional questions regarding this initiative\, 
 please contact digitalinclusion@durhamnc.gov
LOCATION:MakerLab\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan Koslofsky":MAILTO:mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
