SUMMARY:Caring for the Caregiver: Stress Management\, Self-Care\, and Mental Health
DESCRIPTION:Caring for the Caregiver: Stress Management\, Self-Care\, and 
 Mental Health\n\nCaregiving can be rewarding\, but it can also bring 
 emotional and physical stress. Join us for an educational program focused 
 on:\n\n\n	Supporting caregivers’ mental health\n	Recognizing signs and 
 symptoms of caregiver burnout\n	Discovering practical ways to manage stress 
 through self-care and community resources\n\n\nParticipants will learn 
 simple self-care techniques\, including guided breathing and explore 
 strategies for maintaining emotional well-being. The discovery of local and 
 national resources for caregiver support and mental health services will 
 help open new opportunities. Participants will gain tools to aid in their 
 own well-being while caring for others\, through relatable scenarios and 
 group brainstorming.\n\nThis program offers a supportive and judgment-free 
 environment where participation and sharing personal experiences are always 
 optional.\n\nAll caregivers and community members interested in caregiver 
 well-being are welcome.\n\nLed by Amanda Waters an Eastern Carolina 
 University Master’s program student in Nursing Education. She has been a 
 registered nurse for 10 years with experience is in Neurology\, Surgical 
 Trauma\, Intensive Care Units\, Postoperative Surgery\, and Vascular 
 Access. She believes that treating the body as a whole is the most 
 beneficial to the patient and their loved ones. \n\n\n\nNovember 20th 
 starting at 1:30 pm in room 3214 on the third floor of the Durham County 
 Main Library located at 300 North Roxboro Street.\n\nRegister to receive an 
 email reminder about the program\, however registration is not 
 required.\n\nParking is available in the library parking lot or at the 
 North Queen Street Garage located at 115 North Queen Street which is behind 
 the apartments directly across the street from the library. Parking at the 
 garage is free. Please bring your parking ticket to a service point for 
 validation. You can validate your parking ticket before the program. 
 \n\nQuestions? Call 919-560-9311 or email Megan at mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
LOCATION:Conference Room #3214\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Megan Koslofsky":MAILTO:mkoslofsky@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:Classes & Lectures, Durham, Health & Fitness, Social
UID:LibCal-14288-17815595
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17815595
END:VEVENT
