DTSTAMP:20261120T000000Z
SUMMARY:Mahalia Jackson\, Moving On Up a Little Higher: A Social Justice Conversation
DESCRIPTION:If Americans remember Mahalia Jackson at all\, they know her as 
 the greatest gospel singer to ever live—but she was also much more. In 
 their new revisionist biography\, New York Times bestselling author Timothy 
 B. Tyson and acclaimed gospel singer Mary D. Williams pluck Jackson from 
 obscurity and rightfully place her back in the spotlight\, restoring her 
 status as a major civil rights figure. She was not only the soundtrack to 
 the Civil Rights Movement\, but a political advisor to Dr. Martin Luther 
 King\, Jr. \, a local activist\, and prolific fundraiser. \n\nJoin us for a 
 musical performance and a groundbreaking dialogue\, with noted social 
 justice advocate and journalist Dr. Benjamin F. Chavis\, Jr and authors Tim 
 Tyson and Mary D. William in discussing the socio-political life and 
 humanitarian worldview of Mahalia Jackson in American life. Several Durham 
 area pastors and activists were close personal friends and acquaintances of 
 Dr. King and Mahalia Jackson.\n\nThis event is sponsored by the Durham 
 County Library\, NC Council of Churches\, John Hope Franklin Research 
 Center at Duke\,  OLLI at Duke\, Live Right|W.W. Norton\, The Regulator 
 Bookshop\, The Fruit of Labor Singing Ensemble and Durham Crisis Response 
 Center. A book signing with the authors will follow the event.
LOCATION:Main Library - Auditorium - Upper Corridor 2nd Floor\, Main Library (300 N. Roxboro St)
ORGANIZER;CN="Carter Cue":MAILTO:ccue@dconc.gov
CATEGORIES:
UID:LibCal-14288-17851394
URL:https://durhamcountylibrary.libcal.com/event/17851394
END:VEVENT
